{
  "slug": "auto-approve-compound-bash",
  "name": "Auto Approve Compound Bash",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Auto-approve compound Bash commands (pipes, chains, subshells) by parsing each segment via shfmt AST and checking against allow/deny lists",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 hook**, `PreToolUse`.\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install auto-approve-compound-bash@claude-community` from `oryband/claude-code-auto-approve`.\n\nA Claude Code hook that auto-approves compound Bash commands when every sub-command is in your allow list and none are in your deny list.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
